00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.230
Jack: In general, the world has
become a place where most people

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:07.160
communicate in short sound bites
limited by word counts via social media.

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:11.379
It is easier to communicate via
text than to engage in conversation.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:15.690
Verbal communication styles have
subsequently had to adapt to meet

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:19.779
these restrictions by being clear and
concise to get a message over quickly.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.979
However, some messages are more
complicated and cannot be communicated

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.909
in that way but can still be
explained clearly and concisely.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:32.860
They also must be interesting enough to
engage the listener and informative enough

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:34.769
to enable the listener to understand.

00:00:35.559 --> 00:00:39.229
Leah: One way of engaging listeners
is to take a storytelling approach

00:00:39.489 --> 00:00:41.039
to put a message into context.

00:00:41.749 --> 00:00:45.499
Learning to express information as a
story can help to draw the listeners

00:00:45.519 --> 00:00:50.089
in by having a beginning a middle and
an end, rather than just expressing

00:00:50.099 --> 00:00:51.859
a list of facts and information.

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:56.200
Even introducing characters and
scenarios can make it more interesting.

00:00:56.610 --> 00:01:00.980
Using metaphors and analogies can
also help put across complex messages

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:02.830
that may not be easy to explain.

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:07.119
They can also link it to something that
the listener may be more accustomed

00:01:08.389 --> 00:01:08.409
Jack: to.

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:12.179
Using visual aids can also help with
presentations to demonstrate ideas,

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:14.869
give examples and reinforce information.

00:01:14.869 --> 00:01:19.750
A clear and easy to understand speaking
voice can help engage listeners and

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:23.329
keep them actively listening, especially
knowing when to change tone and

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:25.619
inflection and pausing for reactions.

00:01:25.889 --> 00:01:26.189
One of the

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:29.949
Leah: most important things when
presenting information and ideas is

00:01:29.949 --> 00:01:31.632
to be prepared and plan what is to be
communicated verbally, whether this is by

00:01:31.632 --> 00:01:31.635
use of cue cards or visual presentation.

00:01:31.635 --> 00:01:31.643
Otherwise, important information
may be omitted or misrepresented

00:01:31.643 --> 00:01:31.659
with potentially damaging effects.

